Or if you must, zap on the diagonal, like this:


------------- (wall)
     /\
    /  \
   /    \
  /      @ (you)

Unless I'm greatly mistaken, the beam of fire will always follow the
indicated path and won't hit you.

Or just stand far enough away from the wall that it won't bounce back
and hit you. But you might as well get a monster in there, as well -
no point wasting a charge on a nasty attack wand. (Really, the only
wand that it's *bad* to zap at a monster is polymorph, and even then
you could always re-zap it until it changes back into something you
can handle. Invisibility might not be a great idea, either, but unless
it's something really sneaky like a nymph, it's not too difficult to
deal with the result.)

I must confess, I don't really believe in Elbereth-testing. It's not
intuitively obvious, and too spoilerish for my taste (for the same
reason I don't price-ID). There's no way your character in the game
would have either a long list of prices or engraving effects
memorized, and neither do I.

